   Wizard mode is kind of fun every now and then. You didn't mention what
system you're playing on. On a UNIX system wizard more is entered by 
the command 'nethack -D'. 

  Wishing in wizard mode is even better than normal wishing. You can wish
for a +50 broadsword named Stormbringer, a +100 gray dragon scale mail,
or a wand of death (100) and get each of these. You can even wish for the 
amulet of Yendor. 

   In wizard mode you get unlimited intrinsic wishing. Simply type control-W.
That is, press the control key and hold it down while pressing W. You also
can create monster (control-G), map the level (control-F), show the location 
of the special levels (control-O), show your intrinsics (control-X), and
identify objects (control-I). CAVEAT: if you're playing on a UNIX system
you won't be able to enter wizard mode unless your userid was listed as the 
wizard when the game was built.

   In wizard mode you *don't* get a wand of wishing to start. If you do, 
you're in discover mode.

  By the way, using wizard mode is *not* unethical. It doesn't effect the 
score list so people have no right to flame you about it. People do get 
angry when someone uses a cheat, (copying save or level files, stopping
the process to escape from a floating eye, etc.) and *then* claims that 
winning the game that way is as legitimate as normal play. They also would
be a little unhappy if you use wizard mode to create a bones level with 
some of the above mentioned items ;-).




